# server.js is the entry point for a long-lived process — npm start, the
# Dockerfile, Render. Vercel does not need it: api/index.js is the entry there,
# and nothing the function requires reaches this file.
#
# It has to be kept out of the upload rather than just unused, because leaving it
# there was actively harmful. Vercel's Node detection built it into a second
# function and mounted that at /, so the landing page bypassed api/index.js
# entirely: it imported the app at module scope, which crashes the whole
# invocation on any configuration error instead of answering with the reason, and
# it had none of the includeFiles from vercel.json, so it could not have read a
# page out of views/ even once the database was reachable.
server.js

# Nothing here is needed to serve a request.
test
.github
render.yaml
Dockerfile
